course: dictionary
lesson: 7604
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. Print is one of them: it can be a verb (something you do) or a noun (something you can see or hold). Read the words around it to find out which meaning you need. Context is your best clue.
explain: «The small print at the bottom of the advert was hard to read.» Small print is writing made by a machine in tiny letters, so here print is a noun. When you see «printed» or «printing» near a machine, paper or a picture, it probably means putting words or pictures onto paper.
explain: Print can also mean a mark left by pressing. «Small birds such as sparrows leave pairs of prints in the mud.» These prints are like footprints: a bird's feet pressed into the mud and left a shape behind. Ask yourself: what is pressing, and what is left behind?
fact: Print can be a verb (print, prints, printed, printing) or a noun (print, prints).
fact: To print is to put words or pictures onto paper with a machine.
fact: Small print is writing made by a machine in tiny letters, often for rules.
fact: A print is a mark left by pressing, like a footprint or fingerprint.
fact: A print can also be a copy of a picture or photo.
exercise: «Please print your homework before Friday.» What does print mean here? | To read quietly | *To put words onto paper with a machine | To write letters by hand, not joined up | To press your feet into mud
exercise: «The detective found a clear print on the glass.» In this sentence, print is a | Verb, like to print | Kind of tiny letter | *Noun, a mark left by pressing | Machine for making paper
exercise: «Read the small print before you sign.» What does small print mean? | A short poem | Letters written quickly by hand | Pictures drawn very small | *Rules written in tiny letters
test: «She printed three copies of the photo.» What does printed mean? | Folded them neatly into a box | Read them aloud slowly | *Made copies on paper with a machine | Pressed her feet into the sand
test: «Birds left prints in the snow.» Which meaning of prints fits best? | Copies of a picture | Machine-made writing | Small rules | *Marks left by pressing
exam: Which sentence uses print as a noun? | The machine can print in colour. | *The detective studied the print on the window. | The printer will print ten copies before lunch. | We need to print the map for the trip.
